WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.466
Hey, Dreamer here, back in the workshop.

4
00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:13.129
Last time you learned your way around Studio.

5
00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:19.222
This time we give our world its voice: the three spots the narrator reads before it says a single word.

6
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:25.331
Through this whole series we build one world from scratch, and it's my travelling show.

7
00:00:25.331 --> 00:00:29.380
A circus caravan rolling from town to town, and you join as the newest act.

8
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.456
I've already typed this episode's bits in, so you don't have to watch me type for ten minutes.

9
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:38.371
First stop: Story, then Story Overview.

10
00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.683
The top box is the world background.

11
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:44.600
Think of it as the one page the narrator keeps in its pocket.

12
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.389
What the world is, who you are, and what keeps going wrong.

13
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:51.097
Every box has a little info icon.

14
00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:57.889
This one says the story and the other AI jobs all lean on it, so only put in things that stay true.

15
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.577
Under it is quest generation guidance.

16
00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:04.593
When Voyage makes up a job on the fly, this is the brief it follows.

17
00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:09.967
Mine says keep jobs small and close to the road, and let them go wrong in funny ways first.

18
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:16.439
Voyage's own guide says it goes into almost every prompt, so every word fights for room.

19
00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:22.146
Start with the genre and the hook, then what's happening right now, then where the player comes in.

20
00:01:22.146 --> 00:01:26.124
Mine opens with road-show fantasy, loud, goofy and slightly unhinged,

21
00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:28.603
and you can feel the whole world from that.

22
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.421
Next, Narrator Style.

23
00:01:31.421 --> 00:01:34.806
This is how the narrator talks, not what it knows.

24
00:01:34.806 --> 00:01:40.762
Mine is third person, present tense, fast and loud, but when danger comes it lands hard.

25
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.298
The default narrator already talks in third person,

26
00:01:45.298 --> 00:01:48.491
present tense, so only say it if yours is different.

27
00:01:48.491 --> 00:01:52.606
Then how it should feel, how strangers act, and a short never list.

28
00:01:52.606 --> 00:01:57.211
Mine says never save the player from a bad call, no matter how funny it is.

29
00:01:57.211 --> 00:02:00.650
The box holds two thousand characters, so keep it tight.

30
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.592
Last one: World Lore.

31
00:02:03.592 --> 00:02:07.525
Each entry is one thing that's true about your world.

32
00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:10.217
The plus button adds a new entry.

33
00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:11.717
I've already made two.

34
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.795
Open one and there's a name and the text.

35
00:02:14.795 --> 00:02:19.410
Here's the trick: the narrator only ever reads the text, never the name.

36
00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:24.218
So the text has to say what it's about, right there in the first few words.

37
00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:29.220
Private, source summary I D and story sequence come from Voyage's memory system.

38
00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.806
The game fills them in on memories it writes as the story goes,

39
00:02:32.806 --> 00:02:37.075
and Private keeps one of those from being shared with the other characters.

40
00:02:37.075 --> 00:02:40.091
For lore you write yourself, the text is what counts.

41
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.405
The best lore entries are rules.

42
00:02:43.405 --> 00:02:45.549
What happens when something happens.

43
00:02:45.549 --> 00:02:50.728
Mine says the show feeds its own, and anyone who sells it out wakes up without a wagon.

44
00:02:50.728 --> 00:02:54.598
Voyage finds an entry when it's relevant, wherever the player is,

45
00:02:54.598 --> 00:02:57.754
and the narrator uses it without reading it out loud.

46
00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.818
That's our world's voice.

47
00:03:00.818 --> 00:03:04.648
Everything from this episode is linked in the description,

48
00:03:04.648 --> 00:03:07.619
so paste it into a test world and poke at it.

49
00:03:07.619 --> 00:03:11.647
Next time, quests, and how a quest actually reaches a player.

50
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.048
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

